From 315089177fe1636ab5a8e40992246c4fdbd0c711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:28:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): refuse carrying stock between setups on
 different machines

The program sim checked only the active setup's machine kind, so a carry
(or clip) across a machine change was judged unrefused, against what the
#401 notes said. The machine is now each setup's own (#343):

- carry::entry refuses a carry onto another machine by name
  (CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL, naming both setups and both machines), so the
  rest reading (#318) refuses it at generation too; the lathe/mill-turn
  gate reads the setups' shared machine instead of the active one's.
- carry::walk (simulate_document, incoming_body) refuses every setup
  change onto another machine, the M3.2 A clip included.

Pins carried-grid alignment for an odd cell count under an off-grid
translation, in the engine (7 x 5 lattice, flip and quarter turn
translated by (0.37, -1.13)) and in the app (a flip about a part centre
off the grid pitch): every image cell centre is a transformed source
centre, origin and bounds exact, nothing shifted.

Decisions: docs/decisions/404-carry-machine-check.md.

Fixes #404

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
